        "comments": "The assembly csSphFimb3.1 is based on 57x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Order and orientation of scaffolds on chromosome 21 from\n1.58-1.76Mb and chromosome 22 from\n1.17-1.72Mb is unsure. Chromosomes 21 and 22 are microchromosomes which based on coverage are likely underepresented in copy number in this assembly.",
